<section xml:id="materials" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Course Materials</title>

  <introduction><p>The following is a list of primary resources for the course. 
  There may be additional readings distributed during the course.</p></introduction>

  <subsection xml:id="SS_reqtext"><title>Required Texts</title>

  <p>These text are available through the Linfield Bookstore.
    <ul>
    <li><pubtitle> Prisoner's Dilemma</pubtitle>, Poundstone, Doubleday, 1992.</li>

    <!--<li><pubtitle>The Mind Game</pubtitle>, MacDonald, Ballantine Books, 2000.</li>-->

    <li><pubtitle>They Say I Say</pubtitle>, 6th ed.,  Graff and Birkenstein, Norton, 2024.</li>

  </ul></p>

</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="SS_readings"><title>Other Readings</title></subsection>

<p>These articles will be distributed in the course.
  <ul>
    <li><q>Battles of Wits and Matters of Trust: Game Theory in Popular Culture,</q> Nordstrom,  
    <pubtitle>Mathematics and Popular Culture: Essays on Appearances in Film, Literature, Gaming, Television and Other 
    Media</pubtitle>, eds, E. Sklar and J. Sklar, McFarland, 2012.</li>

    <li><q>Game Theory and Literature,</q> Brams, <pubtitle>Games and Economic Behavior</pubtitle> ,  
    <alert>6</alert>, 32-54, 1994.</li>

    <li><q>The Tale of Happiton,</q>  <pubtitle>Metamagical Themas: Questing for the Essence of Mind and Pattern</pubtitle>, 
    Hofstadter, Basic Books, 1985.</li>
  </ul>
</p>

<subsection xml:id="SS_reqfilm"><title>Required Films</title>

<p>These films are available to borrow in the Linfield Library. You may also watch them through your own services. If requested, I can arrange a group showing of these films.
  <ul>
    <li><pubtitle>Dr. Strangelove</pubtitle> (1964)</li>
    <li><pubtitle>Return to Paradise</pubtitle> (1998)</li>
    <li><pubtitle>The Dark Knight</pubtitle> (2008)</li>
    <li><pubtitle>Crazy Rich Asians</pubtitle> (2018)</li>
    <li><pubtitle>Footloose</pubtitle> (1984)</li>
  </ul>
</p>
</subsection>


  
</section>
